      <article class="fqc rv" id="faq-which-systems-can-you-look-after"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Which systems can you look after?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>In care</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="igq1"><span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-team"/></svg></i><b>CRM</b><em>Yes</em></span><span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-sheet"/></svg></i><b>ERP</b><em>Yes</em></span><span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-code"/></svg></i><b>Custom web app</b><em>Yes</em></span><span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-pin"/></svg></i><b>Mobile app</b><em>Yes</em></span><span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-link"/></svg></i><b>Integrations</b><em>Yes</em></span><span class=x><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-search"/></svg></i><b>Built elsewhere</b><em>Check first</em></span></div></div></div><p>CRM, ERP, custom web apps, mobile apps and integrations, whether we built them or not. If someone else built a system, we check it first and tell you if anything needs fixing before care can start.</p></div></div></article>
      <article class="fqc rv open" id="faq-how-much-does-system-care-cost"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="true"><span>How much does system care cost?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Prices</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-card"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="xsq2"><div><b>System Care</b><small>1 system · monitoring + bug fixes · 1.5 h</small><em>RM399/mo</em></div><div class="on"><b>System Care Plus</b><small>Up to 3 · monthly health review · 5 h</small><em>RM999/mo</em></div><div><b>System Priority</b><small>Up to 6 · priority queue + report · 10 h</small><em>RM1,999/mo</em></div></div></div></div><p>System Care is RM399 a month for 1 system or integration, with monitoring, bug fixes and 1.5 support hours. System Care Plus is RM999 for up to 3 systems, adds a monthly health review and 5 hours. System Priority is RM1,999 for up to 6 systems, with a priority queue, a monthly report and 10 hours.</p></div></div></article>
      <article class="fqc rv" id="faq-what-counts-as-a-system"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>What counts as a system?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Counting</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-sheet"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="igq3"><p><span><b>ERP or CRM</b><small>One installation</small></span><em class="g">1 system</em></p><p><span><b>Web app or mobile app</b><small>One app with its admin view</small></span><em class="g">1 system</em></p><p><span><b>Integration</b><small>One connection between tools</small></span><em class="g">1 system</em></p></div></div></div><p>One ERP or CRM, one web app, one mobile app with its admin view, or one integration each counts as one system. The same app on iPhone and Android counts once.</p></div></div></article>
      <article class="fqc rv" id="faq-what-do-support-hours-cover"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>What do support hours cover?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Support hours</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="igq3"><p><span><b>Bug fixes</b><small>Things that used to work</small></span><em class="g">Yes</em></p><p><span><b>Updates and patches</b><small>Security and versions</small></span><em class="g">Yes</em></p><p><span><b>New features</b><small>Quoted separately</small></span><em class="g">Quoted</em></p></div></div></div><p>Fixing bugs, applying updates and patches, small configuration changes and the monthly review. New features and major upgrades are quoted separately. Unused hours don’t roll over.</p></div></div></article>
      <article class="fqc rv" id="faq-is-support-24-7"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Is support 24/7?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Response</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="igq3"><p><span><b>Business hours</b><small>Mon–Fri, 9–6</small></span><em class="g">All plans</em></p><p><span><b>Priority queue</b><small>Your tickets go first</small></span><em class="g">Priority</em></p><p><span><b>24/7 emergency SLA</b><small>Not included</small></span><em class="g">No</em></p></div></div></div><p>No. System care runs in business hours and doesn’t include a 24/7 emergency SLA. With System Priority, your tickets go to the front of our queue. Maintenance work is done in an agreed window outside your busy hours.</p></div></div></article>
      <article class="fqc rv" id="faq-is-hosting-included"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Is hosting included?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Separate</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-globe"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="igq1"><span class=x><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-globe"/></svg></i><b>Hosting and servers</b><em>Separate</em></span><span class=x><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg></i><b>Licences</b><em>Separate</em></span><span class=x><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-link"/></svg></i><b>API fees</b><em>Separate</em></span><span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg></i><b>Renewal reminders</b><em>Included</em></span></div></div></div><p>No. Hosting, servers, software licences and API fees are paid to your providers. We keep track of what’s due and remind you before renewals.</p></div></div></article>
      <article class="fqc rv" id="faq-when-does-system-care-start"><button class="fqq" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>When does system care start?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fqx"><div><div class="pv"><div class="wg"><div class="wt"><span>Timeline</span><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-cal"/></svg></i><i><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ne"/></svg></i></div><div class="igq3"><p><span><b>Our builds</b><small>After the 30, 60 or 90-day defect support</small></span><em class="g">Then care</em></p><p><span><b>Other systems</b><small>After an onboarding check</small></span><em class="g">Then care</em></p></div></div></div><p>For systems we build, care usually starts when the included defect support ends: 30, 60 or 90 days after launch depending on the package. For other systems, it starts after a short onboarding check.</p></div></div></article>
